  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "In July 2012, Bombardier Aerospace announced a temporary production pause of the latest Learjet 60XR, set to begin in the fourth quarter of 2012.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383972529:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On the earlier Longhorn wing, interference between the winglet and the wing nearly canceled the effects of the winglet.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383972529:15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The Learjet 60 is a mid-size, medium-range business jet that Bombardier Aerospace manufactured in Wichita, Kansas, United States.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383972529:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Readers also turned to the 2026 Palm Beach County Learjet 60 crash article, with 220,959 readers, and to the Learjet article, with 64,003.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_Palm_Beach_County_Learjet_60_crash:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:Learjet:2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:34Z",
      "text": "On 2 November 2026, 263,003 people read the Learjet 60 article, about 2,210× the usual.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Learjet_60:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:Learjet_60:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:41Z",
      "text": "Readers used 9 languages, and after English, German was the most common, with 17,154 readers.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Learjet_60:2026-11-02",
        "views:de:Learjet_60:2026-11-02"
